ECT_DIR. Every Claude Code machine has ~/.claude, so a hook-input cwd under $HOME but outside any project (for example a directory added with --add-dir) resolves the \"project root\" to $HOME.\n- Effects in that case: plan, ceremony and ledger lookups run against ~/.claude/plans and git runs in $HOME. When CEO_CONTEXT_PROGRESS_FLOOR_TOKENS is set, the hysteresis marker is written under ~/.claude/state.\n- The git-toplevel fallback also uses a fixed 2.0 s timeout outside the TIME_BUDGET_S deadline that gate() computes beforehand.\n- Impact is low (advisory hook, edge-case cwd), and the code may predate this delta.\n- Fix: when cwd is inside CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR, prefer it; stop the walk-up before $HOME; pass the remaining budget to the fallback _git call.\n\nVERDICT: GO This payload's moved code binds and resolves correctly, keeps its fail-open direction, ships to adopters, and contradicts none of the declared conditions. The only P1, the profiler's isolation missing CEO_AUDIT_LOG_PATH, appears to predate the move and goes to the annex rather than blocking.\n","numLines":53,"startLine":1,"totalLines":53}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01H3CmBwXTtBL3bFApzrXPbX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
